# Canonicality of little-endian digits: a byte string of a given width is the
# specification's digit expansion of the number it denotes. This is what makes
# an accepted offset re-encode to exactly the bytes it was read from.

law byte_word_roundtrip:
  for +w: Word(8n)
  {U32.from_nat(U32.to_nat(PD.embed8(w))) == PD.embed8(w) : U32}
